  "comments": "<p>The standard weight of these coins was 2/11 troy ounce (87.3 grains).<br><br><i>1920 obverse die varieties:</i><br><strong>Obverse 3</strong> I of GEORGIVS points between beads, small Head is in high relief, flat neck, wide rim;<br><strong>Obverse 4</strong> I of GEORGIVS points at a bead, large Head is in low relief, slightly hollow neck, narrow rim;<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5cc0259224495.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5cc0259224495.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><i>1921 obverse and reverse die varieties:</i><br><strong>Obverse 3</strong> I of GEORGIVS points between beads;<br><strong>Obverse 4</strong> I of GEORGIVS points between beads;<br><strong>Obverse 5</strong> I of GEORGIVS points at a bead;<br><strong>Reverse D</strong> Tail tuft points between the I and M of IMP;<br><strong>Reverse E</strong> Tail tuft points at the left leg of the M of IMP;<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5cc025a6891b2.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5cc025a6891b2.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><i>1926 obverse die varieties:</i><br><strong>Obverse 5</strong> First effigy, round pearls (peas around border) <i>KM#816a</i><br><strong>Obverse 6</strong> Modified effigy, oblong pearls (beans) around border <u>KM#829</u><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5c69369fdb1b3.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5c69369fdb1b3.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>The images above are reproduced with kind permission of<br>Numista member Sjoelund and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer ugc\" href=\"http://www.declanmageecoins.co.uk/G5S.html\">Declan Magee Coins</a></p>",
